easywall on FenrirOS
====================

Installed inert: neither service is enabled, there is no account and no
password.

    dinitctl enable easywall-web      # starts easywall-setup and easywall-core first

On the first start easywall-setup copies the default configuration from
/usr/share/easywall/*.toml.template to /etc/easywall/ (the web configuration
gets a random session key for this machine). Then open https://<host>:12227:
whoever gets there first runs the first-run wizard and chooses the account.
Do this at once, on a trusted network; until then the port answers on every
interface.

Every apply is undone after 120 seconds unless you confirm it in the browser,
so a bad rule cannot lock you out. easywall-core keeps its own nftables table
(inet easywall); rules from firewalld or other tools are not the same table:
run one firewall manager, not both. The kernel needs the nftables options in
linux r3 or later (log, limit, redirect and the other expressions).

easywall-selftest (a systemd one-shot upstream) is not packaged: without it
the core reports "unprovable" for its throwaway-namespace rule test.
